    "chunk_text": "5. ( I) Any moneys which by virtue o f the provisions o fthe First Schedule to this Act, have been allocated to Recurrent Expenditure under any Programme appearing under any Head specified in that Schedule, but have not been expended or are not likely to be expended, may be transferred to the allocation of Capital Expenditure within that Programme or to the allocation o f Recurrent Expenditure or Capital Expenditure under any other Programme within that Head, by Order o f the Secretary to the Treasury or any other officer authorised by him.\n\nPayment from the Consolidated Fund or any other fund or moneys of or al the disposal of the Government, of advances for expenditure on !he activities referred to in section 3, during the financial year 2008.\n\nPower lo transfer unexpended moneys allocated lo Recurrent Expenditure, to another allocation within the same Programme or lo another Programme under the same Head of expenditure.\n\nApproprimion Act, No. 61 of 2007 5\n\n(3) Any Order made under subsection (I) shall, i f so expressed therein. be deemed to have had effect from such date prior to the date of making such Order as may be specified therein.\n\n9. Parliament may by resolution amend the Second Schedule to this Act, by adding to the appropriate Columns of that Schedule any activity and providing for -\n\n(a) all or any \u00b7of the maximum limits relating to such activity;\n\n(b) the minimum limit relating to such activity.\n\nIO. In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhala and Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\nPower of Parli:iment to amend 1hc Second Schedule to 1his Act.\n\nSinhal:i text to prevail in c:ise of inconsistency."
