    "chunk_text": "23.(1) Any contract entered with on behalf of theInstitute may be made as follows:\u2014\n\n(a)if made between private persons, would by law berequired to be in writing, may be made on behalf ofthe Institute in writing under the common seal ofthe Institute;\n\n(c)if made between private persons, would by law bevalid though made orally and not reduced intowriting, may be made orally on behalf of the Instituteby any person or persons duly authorized theretoby the Institute.\n\n(2) A contract made according to this section shall beeffectual in law and shall bind the Institute and all personsthereto and their legal representatives.\n\n24.Any expense incurred by the Institute in any suit orprosecution brought by or against the Institute before anycourt shall be paid out of the funds of the Institute and anycost paid to be recovered by the Institute in any suit orprosecution shall be credited to the Fund of the Institute.\n\n25.(1) No civil or criminal proceedings shall beinstituted\u2014\n\n(a)against the Institute for any lawful act which ingood faith is done or purported to be done by theInstitute under this Act; or\n\nRecovery ofexpensesincurred by theInstitute.\n\nContracts.\n\nProtection ofacts done underthis Act or onthe directions ofthe Institute.\n\n15Institute of Certified Management Accountantsof Sri Lanka Act, No. 23 of 2009\n\nNo writ to issueagainst personor property of amember of theCouncil.\n\nOffences andpenalties.\n\nSinhala text toprevail in caseof inconsistency.\n\n(b)against any member, officer, servant or agent forany act which in good faith is done or purported tobe done by such member, officer, servant or agentunder this Act or on the directions of the Council,as the case may be.\n\n(2) Any expense incurred by any person specified insubsection (1) in any suit or prosecution brought againstsuch person before any Court for any act done under this Actor on the direction of the Institute shall if the Courtdetermines that such act was done in good faith be paid outof the Fund of the Institute."
