    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nNATIONAL POLICE ACADEMY\n\nACT, No. 44 OF 2011\n\nPrinted on the Order of Government\n\n[Certified on 21st November, 2011]\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 13.00Postage : Rs. 15.00\n\nPublished as a Supplement to Part II of the Gazette of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka of November 25, 2011\n\n1National Police Academy Act, No. 44 of 2011\n\n2\u2014PL 006260\u20144,090 (09/2011)\n\n[Certified on 21st November, 2011]\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 39/2010.\n\nAN ACT TO PROVIDE FOR THE ESTABLISHMENT OF A NATIONAL POLICEACADEMY; TO IDENTIFY THE OBJECTIVE AND FUNCTIONS OF, AND TO\n\nPROVIDE FOR THE MANAGEMENT AND ADMINISTRATION OF THENATIONAL POLICE ACADEMY; AND TO PROVIDE FOR MATTERS\n\nCONNECTED THEREWITH OR INCIDENTAL THERETO.\n\nBE it therefore enacted by the Parliament of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the National Police AcademyAct, No. 44 of 2011.\n\nPART I\n\nESTABLISHMENT OF THE NATIONAL POLICE ACADEMY\n\n2.(1) There shall be established an academy, whichshall be called the \u201cNational Police Academy\u201d (hereinafterreferred to as \u201cthe Academy\u201d).\n\n(2) The Academy shall, by the name assigned to it bysubsection (1) be a body corporate and shall have perpetualsuccession and a common seal and may sue and be sued insuch name.\n\n3.The Secretary to the Ministry of the Minister assignedthe administration of the Police Department, shall be chargedwith the responsibility of ensuring the efficient managementand administration of the Academy in order to achieve theobjective for which the Academy is established.\n\n4.The objective of the Academy shall be to developthe professional knowledge and skills of police officers andother law-enforcement officers selected for training at the\n\nShort title.\n\nEstablishmentof the NationalPoliceAcademy."
